        "workflow": {
          "name": "archon-pr",
          "description": "Open a pull request for the committed work on the current branch — draft by\ndefault when composed, template-aware, with the body built from the run's\nartifacts — or push to the one it already has. Pushes and verifies by reading\nthe pull request back. When its caller allows it, it also publishes content the\nrun prepared for the description as a marked section of it, and reads that back.\nIt runs no validation and merges no base: CI judges the pushed head. Never sweeps unrelated changes, never rebases and never\nforce-pushes.\n\nUse when: committed work on a branch needs a PR — \"open a PR\", \"create a\ndraft PR for this branch\".\nNOT for: implementing (implement), reviewing (review), or merging (always human).\n",
          "model": "medium",
          "nodes": [
